.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NQKMEINI 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqkmhlen ,
.Nm nqkmpeek ,
.Nm nqkmeini ,
.Nm nqkmeupd ,
.Nm nqkmefin ,
.Nm nqkmdini ,
.Nm nqkmdupd ,
.Nm nqkmdfin
.Nd a stream sealed to several ML-KEM public keys, signed or not
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Vt typedef struct { nqkalg alg; const uint8_t *pk; size_t pklen; } nqkrcp;
.Ft int
.Fn nqkmhlen "const nqkrcp *r" "size_t n" "size_t *hlen"
.Ft int
.Fo nqkmpeek
.Fa "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n" "size_t *hlen" "nqsalg *sig"
.Fa "size_t *nrcp"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkmeini
.Fa "nqkmctx *c" "const nqkrcp *r" "size_t n" "nqsalg sig"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen" "uint32_t chunk"
.Fa "uint8_t *hdr" "size_t cap" "size_t *hlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkmeupd
.Fa "nqkmctx *c" "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkmefin
.Fa "nqkmctx *c" "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkmdini
.Fa "nqkmctx *c" "nqkalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *hdr" "size_t hlen" "uint32_t *chunk" "nqsalg *sig"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkmdupd
.Fa "nqkmctx *c" "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkmdfin
.Fa "nqkmctx *c" "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions seal a stream of any length, in chunks, to up to
.Dv NQKMRCP
(64) ML-KEM public keys at once, so that the secret key of any one of
them opens it, and let its sender sign it.
The format is noqtis-kstream-2; the stream to one key, not signed, is
that of
.Xr nqkfeini 3 .
.Ss The format
The stream is the STREAM construction of
.Xr nqkfeini 3
on ChaCha20-Poly1305, under a random 32-byte file key.
The header is
.Dv NQKMFIX
(24) bytes, then one entry for each recipient:
.Bl -column "offset" "bytes" "what"
.It Sy offset Ta Sy bytes Ta Sy what
.It 0 Ta 4 Ta Ql NQKM
.It 4 Ta 1 Ta the version, 2
.It 5 Ta 1 Ta the flags: bit 0 set when the stream is signed
.It 6 Ta 4 Ta the chunk size, big-endian
.It 10 Ta 7 Ta a random nonce prefix
.It 17 Ta 1 Ta the signature algorithm (its Vt nqsalg ) , 0 when not signed
.It 18 Ta 2 Ta the number of recipients, big-endian
.It 20 Ta 4 Ta the whole header's length, big-endian
.El
.Pp
An entry is the recipient's KEM (its
.Vt nqkalg ,
one byte), the first 8 bytes of the SHA3-256 of its public key, the
ML-KEM ciphertext, and the file key under ChaCha20-Poly1305 with a nonce
of zeros (48 bytes).
The key that wraps the file key is HKDF-SHA-256 of the shared secret,
with no salt and the info
.Ql noqtis-kwrap-2 ,
the SHA3-256 of the recipient's public key, the context's length (one
byte) and the context, the 24 fixed bytes, and the KEM ciphertext.
The stream's key is HKDF-SHA-256 of the file key, with no salt and the
info
.Ql noqtis-kstream-2 ,
the context's length and the context, and the SHA3-256 of the whole
header: a header changed anywhere, in another recipient's entry too,
gives every recipient another key, and the first chunk fails.
.Pp
Chunk
.Em i
is sealed with the nonce prefix, then
.Em i
(32 bits, big-endian), then 1 for the last chunk and 0 for the others.
A signed stream has one more record after its last chunk, of the
signature's size plus 16 bytes, sealed with the same counter and the
last byte 2: the sender's signature, with the context
.Ql noqtis-kstream-2 ,
of the SHA3-256 of the header's SHA3-256 followed by the whole
plaintext.
The signature is inside the encryption, so only a recipient learns who
signed; it covers the header, so a recipient cannot seal the plaintext
to someone else and keep the sender's signature.
.Ss Sealing
.Fn nqkmhlen
gives in
.Fa *hlen
the header's size for the
.Fa n
recipients
.Fa r .
.Fn nqkmeini
writes the header to
.Fa hdr
.Pq Fa cap No bytes , Fa *hlen No its size, also with Dv NQEBUF ;
.Fa sig
is the algorithm the sender will sign with, or 0 for a stream that is
not signed;
.Fa chunk
is 0 for
.Dv NQKFCHUNK
or
.Dv NQKFCMIN
to
.Dv NQKFCMAX .
.Fn nqkmeupd
seals one full chunk and
.Fn nqkmefin
the last
.Pq Fa n No at most the chunk size ,
each to
.Fa out
with its 16-byte tag.
For a signed stream
.Fn nqkmefin
takes the sender's secret key
.Fa sk
and appends the record:
.Fa out
then needs
.Fa n
+ 16 bytes plus the signature's size + 16.
For a stream that is not signed
.Fa sk
is
.Dv NULL .
.Ss Opening
.Fn nqkmpeek
reads the first
.Dv NQKMFIX
bytes of a stream and gives the header's whole length, the signature
algorithm (0: not signed) and the number of recipients, refusing sizes
out of range before anything is read into them.
.Fn nqkmdini
opens the header
.Pq Fa hlen No exactly that length
with one recipient's secret key
.Fa sk
of
.Fa alg
and gives the chunk size.
.Fn nqkmdupd
opens one chunk of the chunk size plus 16 bytes.
.Fn nqkmdfin
opens the last, whose input, for a signed stream, also holds the record
that follows it, and checks the signature under the sender's public key
.Fa pk .
With
.Fa pk
.Dv NULL
the signature is not checked: the caller does not ask who sent the
stream.
.Pp
A reader gets the plaintext chunk by chunk, before the signature at the
end is checked.
What it wrote is the sender's only once
.Fn nqkmdfin
returned
.Dv NQOK ;
on any error the last chunk's output is wiped, and the earlier chunks
are the caller's to discard.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ,
or:
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Dv NQEARG
An argument out of range: no recipient or more than
.Dv NQKMRCP ,
a context over 255 bytes, a chunk size out of range, a part where a
full chunk is wanted, a key given to
.Fn nqkmefin
for a stream that is not signed or none for one that is.
.It Dv NQEBUF
An output buffer too small; the size wanted is in
.Fa *hlen
or
.Fa *outlen ,
and the stream goes on.
.It Dv NQEDEC
A key of the wrong size; a header that is not noqtis-kstream-2, or
whose entries do not add up to its length; a chunk of the wrong size.
.It Dv NQEVRFY
From
.Fn nqkmdini :
no entry opens with the key (it is not a recipient, or the context is
another).
From
.Fn nqkmdupd
and
.Fn nqkmdfin :
a chunk or the record does not verify; the signature does not verify
under
.Fa pk ;
or
.Fa pk
is given for a stream that is not signed.
.It Dv NQELIM
From
.Fn nqkmpeek :
a number of recipients, a header length or a chunk size out of range.
The 2^32nd chunk of a stream.
.It Dv NQENOSUP
A KEM that is not ML-KEM, or a signature algorithm this library does
not know.
.It Dv NQESTATE
A context used out of order, or after its stream ended.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
